1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[orchestral music playing]

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
[machine guns firing]

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Chrollo]
Forever set, a precious moon is lost.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The others mourn him with ceremony grand.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Rising up to heaven, the mighty moon
of frost...

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
with a melody from the mourning band.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
[theme music playing]

8
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
ASSAULT x AND x IMPACT

9
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
-[brakes screeching]
-[passengers groaning]

10
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
[announcer] Attention, passengers.
We will be making an emergency stop.

11
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
-Please watch your step.
-Wait, did something happen?

12
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Dunno.

13
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
[phone ringing]

14
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Are they here?

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Yeah, it's got to be them!

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
They're the only ones I can think of
who are powerful enough

17
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
to take on a whole crowd on their own!
[cries in pain]

18
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
-[gasps] Hey. Hey!
-[crashing]

19
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Listen! Figure out how many enemies
we're up against!

20
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Do whatever it takes to stop them!

21
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Don't let them
anywhere near this building!

22
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[grumbling] They're late!

23
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Our escorts aren't here?
Their names are Melody and Basho.

24
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Unfortunately, sir, all the traffic
in Yorknew City

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
has come to a grinding halt.
They're probably stuck.

26
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
[Nostrade] [grumbling]
It's dangerous for Neon to be here.

27
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Isn't there any way to get her out?

28
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
[guard] The ambulance we requested
is already on its way.

29
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
It shouldn't be much longer, sir.

30
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
[Nostrade]
Ambulance? Oh, yes, that's right.

31
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[Kurapika] Something's wrong here.

32
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
The man entered the building with Neon
and then called for a doctor...

33
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Wait, sir?

34
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Kurapika, do not leave my daughter's side
until the ambulance arrives. Understand?

35
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
But sir, my assignment
is to kill the Phantom Troupe--

36
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
That was when I thought
Neon would be home already.

37
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Instead, she's here and unconscious,
completely exposed to the Troupe.

38
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
I must ensure her safety.

39
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
I want you here for the time being.

40
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Please, Kurapika.

41
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
I understand.

42
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[assassin snickering]

43
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,000
It's such a pity, isn't it?
They aren't putting up much of a fight.

44
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Well, I guess it was stupid to expect--

45
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
[grunts]

46
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[sirens wailing]

47
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Damn it! They're crazier than I thought.

48
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
They're trying to launch
a full-frontal attack

49
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
with only ten people.

50
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
[doctor] My goodness.

51
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
When the hell did this place turn
into such a damn warzone, huh?

52
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
So, where is the patient?

53
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
[EMTs gasping]

54
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[Bean] I don’t have any reason to believe

55
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
that you aren’t a member
of the Phantom Troupe.

56
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Make just one funny move
and I'll blow your head off.

57
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Follow me.

58
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
I will need to inspect all of you.

59
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
What's that?

60
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Damn you.

61
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
-[indistinct chatter]
-[man] Give me a break!

62
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
[announcer]
All trains have been stopped at this time.

63
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
The safety of our customers
is of utmost importance to us.

64
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
So we ask that you continue
to wait patiently for now

65
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[Gon]
I'm not getting any reception down here.

66
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
And we don't know when the trains
will start moving again.

67
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Then I guess we'll just have to run.

68
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[sighs]

69
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Weren't you hired here as an assassin?

70
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Why don't you quit hiding out
in this room and go fight?

71
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Unless you got too scared
when the Phantom Troupe showed up?

72
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Well, actually, I requested
that Kurapika stay here.

73
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
I understand that he's been hired
by the Ten Dons,

74
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
but I'm a bit worried about my daughter.

75
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
It's fine. I won't sell you out.

76
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
But still, I know you're being paid well,
so I expect you to do your job.

77
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[chuckles]

78
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
He's right,
I really should do something to help out.

79
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
I could patrol the building
at the very least.

80
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
I suppose so.

81
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
But you must come back immediately
if I call on you.

82
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
My daughter's safety takes precedence.

83
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[Kurapika] Yes, sir.

84
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[man 1]
How long do we have to wait?

85
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
[man 2]
Hey, what's going on outside?

86
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
[man 3]
Yeah, I hear explosions nearby!

87
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
When is the auction gonna start?

88
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
What the hell is going on here, anyway?

89
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[stammering]
Please, sir, it shouldn't be much longer.

90
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Is the auction still on or isn't it?

91
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:03,000
[Kurapika] Everyone here is either
a leader or an executive member.

92
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
They're endangering themselves needlessly

93
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
only to prove they aren't afraid
of the Troupe.

94
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Give me back my phone!
I don't know what's happening out there.

95
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
I need my weapons back, too!

96
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
[auctioneer stammering]
As you know, sir, the rule state

97
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
that weapons are banned
during the auction.

98
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[man] What happens if they get inside?

99
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
We fight them with our bare hands?

100
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Kurapika]
It's starting to get chaotic in here.

101
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
If they're not careful,
the auction organizers will lose control

102
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
of the situation before much longer.

103
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[phone vibrating]

104
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Yes. Hello?

105
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
-[Gon] Hey! Kurapika?
-[gasps]

106
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[Gon]
Oh, good! We finally got a hold of you.

107
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
-[Kurapika] Gon?
-Yeah, can you talk right now?

108
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Uh, I'm a little busy.
So I'll have to call you back.

109
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
[Gon] Wait! Just give me a minute!

110
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
I have something I really need
to tell you.

111
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Killua and I found the Troupe.

112
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
-[gasps]
-[Gon] Actually, they kind of caught us.

113
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[Kurapika]
What in the hell were you thinking?

114
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Do you have any idea
how dangerous they are?

115
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
I thought I knew until we met them.

116
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
They're really tough.

117
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
As it stands, we don't have a chance
against them.

118
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
That's why we need your help.

119
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
And we want to help you, too.

120
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[Kurapika] This isn't a game.

121
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
I'm not going to help you
get yourselves killed.

122
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
We found their base.
Wanna know where it is?

123
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
[Kurapika] I have my own sources.

124
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
We learned some of their abilities.
Don't you wanna know about them?

125
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
[Kurapika] That's enough!
Just stay away from the Phantom Troupe!

126
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[Killua] You're the "chain user"
who killed one of them, right?

127
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
You do realize that they're dead set
on finding you?

128
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
But if you won't even consider thinking
of me and Gon as your friends and equals,

129
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
we'll do whatever the hell it takes
to make you help us. [grumbles]

130
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
[Gon] Kurapika...

131
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
One of the Phantom Troupe guys...
he started crying right in front of us.

132
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
He said that he could never forgive
whoever killed his friend.

133
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,000
And then when I saw him do that,
it made me really angry.

134
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
I couldn't forgive them.

135
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Look, we want to stop them too!

136
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
So, please, Kurapika.

137
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
[Kurapika] I'll... call you back later.

138
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
[Killua] But if you won't even consider
thinking of me and Gon

139
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
as your friends and equals...

140
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[Gon] Look! We want to stop them too!

141
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[crowd gasping]

142
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
-[Mafioso 1] Here they come!
-[Mafioso 2] Don't let them escape!

143
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
-[Mafioso 3] I can feel the heat!
-[Mafioso 4] Someone's coming!

144
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
-[Mafioso 5] Does he have a gun?
-[Mafioso 6] Who's stationed here?

145
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
[man] Go! Go back! It's no use.

146
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
The Troupe is too powerful!

147
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
I'm serious. We don't stand
a chance against them.

148
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Do you wanna see how strong they are?
'Cause I can show you!

149
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,000
They're this strong! [laughs maniacally]

150
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Damn it!

151
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
[laughter stops]

152
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[Shalnark] Aww, he broke.

153
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
I need to find my next puppet.

154
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Mafioso] Are you okay? I found the corpse
of one of the assassins!

155
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[gasps]

156
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Someone has already gotten
inside the building!

157
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[Kurapika] Damn.

158
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
-[man 1] Who are these guys?
-[man 2] It's hopeless!

159
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Come on! Get back here and fight!

160
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[sighs] What's going on?
It's me. Where the hell is our backup?

161
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
What are you doing?

162
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:07,000
[Mafioso] They should be there any minute.
And we'll be arriving shortly--

163
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
[grunting in pain]

164
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
[Bean] Is this really happening?

165
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
The 2,000 armed men
that were supposed to assemble here...

166
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Are they all getting killed?

167
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Now what?

168
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
There are Troupe members
inside the building already.

169
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
It's me, Bean!

170
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Get the Ten Dons on the line.
And hurry!

171
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Kurapika] The intruder must be
a member of the Troupe.

172
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
They're trying to steal the rest
of the merchandise

173
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
and avenge their comrade.

174
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
He said he could never forgive
whoever killed his friend.

175
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
[Kurapika] That's what I'm hoping for!

176
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[glass smashing]

177
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:03,000
[man] Hey! Enough already!
Give us the weapons we handed over!

178
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
And do it now!

179
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
[auctioneer]
But, sir, the rules state that--

180
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
To hell with the damn rules,
hear me?

181
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
You know what's happening, don't you?

182
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
I'm not stupid.
You've got professional assassins here.

183
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
I've been seeing them all over the place.

184
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,000
If you're gonna depend on those freaks,
then you might as well let us fight!

185
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
For those of you who don't know,
my name is Zeno Zoldyck.

186
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Zoldyck? Like the famous family
of assassins?

187
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Did the Ten Dons actually call in
these monsters?

188
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,000
At the moment,
one bandit has infiltrated this building.

189
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
[crowd gasping]

190
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
He has already killed a number
of the assassins

191
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
that were hired by your people.

192
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,000
It wouldn't much matter if each of you
was armed to the teeth.

193
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
I could still eliminate the lot of you
in under seven seconds.

194
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
The enemy is every bit as capable.

195
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
[crowd gasping]

196
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
If you understand,
then just shut up and wait.

197
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Disregard if you would rather die.

198
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Well, then?

199
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[Silva] A single strike from behind.
Impressive.

200
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
His bloodlust was only exposed
for a brief instant,

201
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
and barely a trace remains.

202
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[sighs]

203
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I suppose I'll have to use En.

204
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:47,000
although it really is
such an exhausting technique.

205
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Let's start from the roof
and then make our way down.

206
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[Silva]
This building's radius is 100 meters.

207
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Think you can handle it, Dad?

208
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
You fool. I could do 300 meters, easily.

209
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
[cracks knuckles]

210
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,000
One thing is certain.
We're not getting paid enough for this.

211
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[phone vibrating]

212
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Kurapika, you're late!

213
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Hurry back at once
and stay by Neon's side!

214
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Yes, sir. I'm on my way.

215
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Damn it!

216
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
[Chrollo] We meet again.

217
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
[Silva] You remember me?

218
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
[Chrollo] How could I forget?
You did kill one of my people.

219
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[Silva] It wasn't easy.

220
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Now, Dad, be careful.

221
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
He can steal people's abilities.

222
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[gasps]

223
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
[Silva] Huh?

224
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
[panting]

225
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
[Chrollo] Two on one sure is rough.

226
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[Silva] Hmm. Must be a good knife
if it can scratch my skin.

227
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
A mid-era Ben's knife by the looks of it.

228
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Hmm. The shape must mean it's poisoned.

229
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
You all right?

230
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Not a problem.

231
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[Chrollo] Not a problem?

232
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Point one milligrams of that stuff
is more than enough to paralyze a whale.

233
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[Zeno]
So you can steal other people's Nen?

234
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Then you're a Specialist.

235
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:55,000
You might even be a threat if you could
use those stolen powers freely.

236
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:59,000
However, that implies
a higher activation cost.

237
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
You couldn't have gotten
the ability, otherwise.

238
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
If I had to make a guess,

239
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:10,000
you must clear four or five conditions
before stealing an ability.

240
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
[Chrollo] He's right.
The old man's a tough customer.

241
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Trying to meet those conditions
while fighting both of us

242
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
will be difficult indeed,
meaning that you won't be able

243
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,000
to steal our abilities as long
as we keep you engaged in battle.

244
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
That poisoned knife of yours is proof.

245
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
[Chrollo] Right again.
Guess I have no choice.

246
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
-Watch my back, Silva.
-Hmm?

247
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
As soon as I have him pinned down,

248
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
even if you have to kill me,
end him.

249
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Got it.

250
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[Chrollo] He focused his aura
into his hand.

251
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,000
The energy potential will be huge.
I don't have the defenses to block it.

252
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
-[Zeno] Huh.
-[Silva] Hmm.

253
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
SKILL HUNTER: BANDIT'S SECRET

254
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[Zeno] A conjured cloak, eh?

255
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Hmm. This could be trouble.

256
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Even if it's a stolen ability,
it would be reckless to attack

257
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
without knowing what it does.

258
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Or so the average person would think.

259
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
But...

260
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
DRAGON HEAD: LONG-TOU XI-HUA

261
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
DRAGON LANCE

262
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,000
[snickers and yells]

263
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
[Zeno] I see what he's doing.

264
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
He can trap the abilities of others
in the conjured book,

265
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
take them out and use them
any time he pleases.

266
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
But there's a catch.
He can't use those abilities

267
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
unless he holds the book open
the entire time.

268
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
The cloak is also a conjured item.

269
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
It doesn't look like he's planning
to attack,

270
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
but it's obvious that he's attempting
to close the distance between us.

271
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
So, it must be a defensive tool
that can be utilized

272
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
to draw closer to an enemy,
and counter-attack.

273
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
We can lower the risk
if we keep our distance.

274
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
We'll wait for our chance,
then strike!

275
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[Chrollo]
This old man is really something.

276
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
He managed to read my mind in an instant.

277
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Doubt I'd capture him alive.

278
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,000
[Silva] So the ability disappears
whenever he closes the book.

279
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
In any case, he's impressive.

280
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:33,000
He's dodging Dad's attacks by a hair,
all while keeping an eye on me.

281
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
His attacks have improved since last time.

282
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
So we don't have any clue
what he's capable of.

283
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:48,000
If we were to stop him,
we may just have to pay with our lives.

284
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[Chrollo] Huh?

285
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Silva! Do it now!

286
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
[laughs]

287
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
[Silva grunts]

288
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] A thunderous tremor ripped
through Yorknew City.

289
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Kurapika had no idea that those shockwaves
would lead to an unexpected development.

290
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
[theme music playing]

291
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
-[Gon] Coming up, Gon...
-[Killua] And Killua's...

292
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

293
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
-I'm Gon!
-I'm Killua!

294
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

295
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Today, we're introducing Shalnark,
a member of the Troupe

296
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
who's really smart, knowledgeable
and cunning!

297
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
He can put a Nen antenna
right on his targets,

298
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
and control them by phone!

299
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
[both] Black voice!

300
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:18,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Fake and Psyche."

301
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:21,000
-[Gon] Kopitor?
-[Killua] Kotorpi?

302
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Gon] Kortopi!
